  "metadata": {
    "title": "Fabrication And Characterization Of High-Quality Nb/Al-AlOx/Nb Cross-Type Josephson Tunnel Junctions Utilising CMP-based Planarisation Techniques",
    "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.22113590",
    "publication_date": "2026",
    "description": "<p>Raw data from measurements of Josephson Junctions <em>IV-</em>characteristics of two separate wafers (Wafer A and Wafer B) as well as the Dektak stress measurement of a deposited Nb film on a 3 inch Si substrate. The name of the CSV file indicate the design width of the measured JJ, i.e. \"4_2um\" represents a 4.2&micro;m wide JJ. CSV files ending with \"gen\" indicate generator signal, while files ending with \"sig\" indicate voltage response signal of the JJ. In order to convert the generator voltage units to current units, one needs to divide by a resistance <em>R</em>=100Ohm. The folder \"StressMap_NbDeposition\" contains the Dektak stress-measurements for the nine wafer orientations. The data is thoroughly analysed and explained in the paper submitted to the \"Superconducting Science And Technology\"-Journal, a link will be provided once the preprint becomes available on arXiv.</p>",
